---
import BaseLayout from 'zuedocs/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RouterDemo from '../components/RouterDemo.astro';
import { primaryNav, siteConfig } from '../data/docs';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Noria — Maximize your Codex & Claude Code limits"
  description="A smart local proxy that routes Codex and Claude Code sessions across multiple accounts. Use more of your available quota without constantly switching logins."
  siteConfig={siteConfig}
  primaryNav={primaryNav}
>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#content">Skip to content</a>
  <div id="content" class="landing">
    <section class="shell landing-hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="landing-hero__copy">
        <p class="kicker"><span class="kicker__glyph" aria-hidden="true">✳</span> Local smart proxy · Codex & Claude Code</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">More limits.<br /><span>Less logging in.</span></h1>
        <p class="landing-hero__lede">You've got multiple coding accounts. You shouldn't have to keep switching between them. Noria intelligently routes your Codex and Claude Code sessions across your accounts, so you get more out of your available usage and spend less time managing logins.</p>
        <div class="landing-actions">
          <a class="landing-button landing-button--primary" href="/docs/quickstart">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="landing-button landing-button--secondary" href="/docs/architecture">See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="landing-hero__chips"><span>Runs on your machine</span><span>Keeps sessions sticky</span><span>Works with your normal clients</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="landing-hero__visual" aria-label="Illustration: several accounts feeding one local coding workflow">
        <div class="landing-hero__visual-heading"><span class="kicker">One connection. Your whole pool.</span><span class="landing-hero__signal"><i></i> Local</span></div>
        <div class="landing-hero__pool">
          <div class="landing-hero__pool-row"><span class="landing-hero__pool-letter">A</span><div><strong>Account one</strong><small>18m until weekly reset</small></div><span class="landing-hero__pool-track"><i style="width:5%"></i></span><b>5%</b></div>
          <div class="landing-hero__pool-row"><span class="landing-hero__pool-letter">B</span><div><strong>Account two</strong><small>6d until weekly reset</small></div><span class="landing-hero__pool-track"><i style="width:80%"></i></span><b>80%</b></div>
          <div class="landing-hero__pool-row"><span class="landing-hero__pool-letter">C</span><div><strong>Account three</strong><small>12h until weekly reset</small></div><span class="landing-hero__pool-track"><i style="width:32%"></i></span><b>32%</b></div>
        </div>
        <div class="landing-hero__convergence" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><span>↓</span><i></i></div>
        <div class="landing-hero__proxy"><span class="landing-hero__proxy-logo">N</span><span><strong>noria</strong><small>Smart account router</small></span><span class="landing-hero__proxy-status">Routing locally ↗</span></div>
        <div class="landing-hero__convergence landing-hero__convergence--short" aria-hidden="true"><span>↓</span></div>
        <div class="landing-hero__client"><span class="terminal-caret">›_</span><strong>Your Codex / Claude Code session</strong><span>Keep coding as usual.</span></div>
        <p class="landing-hero__visual-foot">Illustrative quotas, not live data</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="landing-strip" aria-label="What Noria does"><div class="shell landing-strip__inner">
      <div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><strong>Spread work across accounts</strong></div>
      <div><span aria-hidden="true">↻</span><strong>Switch when a limit hits</strong></div>
      <div><span aria-hidden="true">⌘</span><strong>Keep using your normal tools</strong></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="shell landing-explainer" aria-labelledby="explain-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="kicker">The idea</p><h2 id="explain-title">One smart layer between you and your limits.</h2><p>Codex and Claude Code each have their own usage windows. When you use several accounts, keeping track of those windows becomes a job of its own. Noria handles the routing instead.</p></div>
      <div class="landing-steps">
        <article><span class="step-index">01</span><span class="step-icon" aria-hidden="true">＋</span><h3>Connect your accounts.</h3><p>Sign in to each Codex or Claude Code account once. Your pool is ready when you need it.</p></article>
        <article><span class="step-index">02</span><span class="step-icon" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><h3>Point your clients at Noria.</h3><p>A one-time configuration sends your normal coding sessions through the local proxy.</p></article>
        <article><span class="step-index">03</span><span class="step-icon" aria-hidden="true">∞</span><h3>Forget account switching.</h3><p>Noria chooses an account for new sessions and switches when a usable one reaches its limit.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="landing-demo-section" aria-labelledby="demo-section-title"><div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading section-heading--horizontal"><div><p class="kicker">Under the hood, made simple</p><h2 id="demo-section-title">A smarter way to spend your limits.</h2></div><p>Which account should get your next session? It's not always the one with the most left. Explore an example.</p></div>
      <RouterDemo />
    </div></section>

    <section class="shell landing-affinity" aria-labelledby="affinity-title">
      <div class="landing-affinity__copy"><p class="kicker">Built for prompt caching</p><h2 id="affinity-title">Smart routing.<br /><span>Sticky sessions.</span></h2><p>Switching accounts on every request would wreck your prompt cache. So Noria doesn't.</p><p>Once a conversation starts on an account, it stays there until that account actually hits an applicable usage limit. Only then does Noria look for another eligible account. The new cache warms up naturally as you continue.</p><a class="landing-inline-link" href="/docs/architecture">Understand session affinity <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <div class="affinity-diagram" aria-label="Illustration of session staying with account A and switching to B only on exhaustion">
        <div class="affinity-diagram__label">Conversation / 07</div>
        <div class="affinity-diagram__row"><span class="affinity-diagram__tag">Account A</span><div class="affinity-diagram__requests"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><span class="affinity-diagram__status">Cache stays warm</span></div>
        <div class="affinity-diagram__event"><span>Quota reached on A</span><span>↓</span></div>
        <div class="affinity-diagram__row affinity-diagram__row--second"><span class="affinity-diagram__tag">Account B</span><div class="affinity-diagram__requests"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><span class="affinity-diagram__status">Continue on B</span></div>
        <p>No round-robin. No switching back just because A resets.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="landing-control-band"><div class="shell landing-control-band__inner">
      <div class="landing-control-band__copy"><p class="kicker">Runs in the background</p><h2>Set it up.<br />Stay in your editor.</h2><p>After setup, launch Codex or Claude Code the way you always do—terminal, supported desktop apps, or your editor. On macOS, the native menu bar shows each account's remaining quota and next reset. All routing happens on your computer.</p><a class="landing-inline-link" href="/docs/quickstart">Set up Noria <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <div class="landing-control-panel" aria-label="Illustrative Noria menu controls"><div class="landing-control-panel__heading"><span class="panel-brand">N</span><strong>Noria</strong><span class="panel-running"><i></i> Running</span></div><div class="landing-control-panel__subhead">ACCOUNT POOL</div><div class="landing-control-panel__account"><span>alice@example.com</span><strong>Weekly 72%</strong></div><div class="landing-control-panel__meter"><i style="width:72%"></i></div><div class="landing-control-panel__account"><span>work@example.com</span><strong>Weekly 15%</strong></div><div class="landing-control-panel__meter"><i style="width:15%"></i></div><div class="landing-control-panel__account"><span>extra@example.com</span><strong>Weekly 58%</strong></div><div class="landing-control-panel__meter"><i style="width:58%"></i></div><div class="landing-control-panel__footer"><span>＋ Add account</span><span>↻ Refresh usage</span></div><p>Example menu · not a screenshot or live quota data</p></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="shell landing-install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
      <p class="kicker">Get started</p><h2 id="install-title">Your accounts are ready.<br /><span>Make them work together.</span></h2><p>Install Noria, add your accounts, and connect your clients once. That's it.</p>
      <div class="landing-install__grid"><div><span>macOS / Linux</span><pre><code>curl -fsSL https://noria.ashray.xyz/install.sh | sh</code></pre></div><div><span>Windows / PowerShell</span><pre><code>irm https://noria.ashray.xyz/install.ps1 | iex</code></pre></div></div>
      <div class="landing-actions"><a class="landing-button landing-button--primary" href="/docs/quickstart">Read the quickstart <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="landing-button landing-button--secondary" href="https://github.com/amxv/noria">View on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      <p class="landing-install__foot">Noria works with accounts you authorize. It can't create extra allowance, and when every eligible account is exhausted you still have to wait for a reset.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
